# Code owners — the owner-review guardrail, Layer 1 (ADR-015, docs/agents/governance.md).
#
# GitHub requests/requires a review from a code owner ONLY when a PR changes a
# file matched below. Everything NOT listed here is intentionally UNOWNED, so the
# vast majority of PRs need zero owner review and helpers/agents ship them on
# green CI. The paths below are the seven owner-gated categories — cost, legal,
# security, trust & safety model, destructive data changes, data-collection /
# privacy posture, and safety/medical-disclaimer copy.
#
# THE TEETH: this file only *requests* review until branch protection on `main`
# is set to "Require review from Code Owners" + "Dismiss stale approvals on new
# commits" + "Do not allow bypassing". With that on, an owned-path PR CANNOT be
# merged until @tonytino approves — no collaborator, bot, admin, or agent can
# satisfy or dismiss it. See the owner checklist in docs/agents/governance.md.
#
# DO NOT edit the path list without keeping .github/scripts/owner-review-paths.mjs
# in sync — tests/unit/check-owner-review.test.ts fails the build if they drift.
# This file is itself owner-owned (via `/.github/` below), so loosening the
# guardrail requires the owner's own review.

